0..75 Comment "// The circle\'s loop space, presented at the term stratum: `Loop(x)` is \"x,"
76..145 Comment "// then the loop\" and `Unloop(x)` \"x, then its inverse\", with the two"
146..220 Comment "// cancellations as rules, so these terms are, one stratum down, the words"
221..296 Comment "// that `Path(Circle, Base, Base)` is in `circle.gandr`, the book\'s circle."
297..371 Comment "// Here the mechanism is stated on terms: the presented integers model the"
372..449 Comment "// circle\'s shape with laws that are conversion (`Winding`), a model over the"
450..521 Comment "// native integers owes its laws and a fold into it rests on them under"
522..597 Comment "// `respects` (`NativeWinding`), and the winding number and spinning are an"
598..678 Comment "// equivalence `Circle ≃ Int` whose round trips, `sect` and `retr`, are proved"
679..720 Comment "// by induction over each presented type."
