7721..7794 Comment "/// The winding number into the native integers, a fold that rests on the"
7795..7852 Comment "/// native model\'s laws. At `Loop(Unloop(x))` it computes"
7853..7924 Comment "/// `turn(unturn(native_wind(x)))`, which conversion does not reduce to"
7925..8001 Comment "/// `native_wind(x)` on a variable; the law `turnUnturn` states exactly that"
8002..8078 Comment "/// path, so `respects` names it for the first rule and `unturnTurn` for the"
8079..8153 Comment "/// second. The loop arms call the model\'s operations rather than spelling"
8154..8232 Comment "/// `n + 1`, so each side the rule relates is the law\'s own endpoint. The fold"
8233..8275 Comment "/// checks and owes what its two laws owe."
